#!/usr/bin/python3 -I
"""sharedbox-web: dashboard + self-service join page. Runs unprivileged.

Identity comes from `tailscale whois <peer ip>`; account creation is done by root
(sharedbox-provision.path) which re-verifies everything this process sends it.

With PUBLIC_URL set it also serves the public front door's pages (invite signup, device login, the
portal under /_box/) on a private unix socket that only sharedbox-gate talks to. There, identity is a
root-minted session token that the gate passes along; root re-verifies it for every action.
With PUBLIC_MODE=cloudflare it is instead the email in the Cloudflare Access token the gate verified; the gate
passes both, and root re-verifies the token itself before any signup or portal action.
"""

